IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ntlsl-dates`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1981 (Northern Territory) -- the Territory's general long service leave Act: who it covers
-- (ss 6, 7), the entitlement after 10 years (s 8), public holidays (s 9), payment when employment ends or the employee
-- dies (s 10), how the pay is worked out and when it is paid (s 11), what counts as continuous service (s 12), leave
-- records (s 14), other work during leave (s 16), contracting out (s 17), offences and the time for prosecution (ss 18,
-- 18A).
--
-- SEAT: the employee (or former employee) to whom the Act gives long service leave; for the questions s 10(3) and
-- s 11(7)(b) raise on a death, the employee's personal representative. "Does the Act cover me? Am I entitled to long
-- service leave, and how many weeks? What must I be paid when my job ends? How is the pay worked out? Does this break
-- count? Was I paid on time?" The employer, the Minister, the authorised person and the court get no seat: the Minister's
-- approvals and exemptions (ss 8(5), 13) and every judgment ("justify", "as soon as practicable", "serious misconduct")
-- are asked as facts, never decided.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list). The rules with deadlines
-- (s 11(6) and s 11(7)(b)) are DEONTIC rules run inside two of the questions; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- Edition: reprint REPL021, as in force at 14 October 2015, from legislation.nt.gov.au (retrieved 6 November 2026), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/Long-Service-Leave-Act-1981-NT-current-reprint-REPL021.txt. No regulations
-- under the Act are deposited (s 7(2)(d) lets them add allowances to "pay").
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 1, 2, 3, 19 (machinery); ss 4, 5 (savings and transitional for the 1965-1974 Ordinances); s 8(5A) (the
-- Minister's revocation: asked as whether an approval is in force); s 15 (the authorised person's investigation; s 15(2)
-- is an employer's duty owed to the authorised person, not to the employee); s 14(1), (3) (the record's contents and a
-- false entry: stated in the records question's description); s 17(2) (stated in the continuity answers through
-- s 12(4)(a), (5)(b)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY. Quotations are from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Northern Territory's Word
-- reprint REPL021 of the Long Service Leave Act 1981, not an official version. Copyright in Northern Territory
-- legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the employee's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- NEGATIVES. JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING, with a NOTHING-kind tag, where it does not
-- answer (rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05, copied in NOTES.md). Sites decided case by case carry a fork number
-- (NOTES.md, fork register).

§ `Long service leave in the Northern Territory: the employee's questions`

-- A yes or a no that the text gives in its own words.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below zero` x MEANS IF x LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE x

-- s 8(1): "1.3 weeks for each completed year of continuous service".
`weeks for each completed year` MEANS 1.3

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Does the Act apply to me (ss 6, 7, 8(4), (5), 13)`

-- s 6(1) "Subject to this Act, where a person is or has been, on or after the commencement of this Act, employed in the
-- Territory, this Act applies to and in relation to the person's employment ...". (2) "This Act does not apply to or in
-- relation to: (a) a person in respect of whom provision for long service leave is made by another law of the Territory,
-- or of the Commonwealth or of a State; (b) a person to whom an award applies making provision for long service leave; or
-- (c) a person employed in an honorary capacity." s 7(1) "employee means a person to whom this Act applies who has entered
-- into or works under a contract of service or apprenticeship with an employer, whether the contract is express or
-- implied, oral or in writing, on salary, wages or piecework rates or as a member of a butty gang, full-time or part-time,
-- or casual, or as an outworker." s 7(3): a share of the employer's earnings, or hiring the tools of the work, does not in
-- itself prevent the person being an employee. s 8(4) "Subject to subsection (5) and section 13, an employee who is
-- entitled to long service leave under this Act shall not be entitled to benefits in the nature of long service leave ...
-- otherwise than under this Act." s 8(5): the Minister may approve an agreement whose benefits are not less favourable;
-- s 13: the Minister may exempt an employer in respect of an employee who has benefits under a scheme not less favourable.
-- The Act commenced on 10 November 1981 (endnotes); a person employed in the Territory today meets s 6(1)'s "on or after".
DECLARE `How the Act applies to me` IS ONE OF
    `the Act applies to me`
    `the Act applies to me, but my long service leave is under the agreement the Minister approved (s 8(4), (5))`
    `the Act applies to me, but the Minister has exempted my employer for me because a long service leave scheme gives me benefits no less favourable (s 13)`
    `the Act does not apply to me: another law of the Territory, the Commonwealth or a State provides my long service leave (s 6(2)(a))`
    `the Act does not apply to me: an award that applies to me provides for long service leave (s 6(2)(b))`
    `the Act does not apply to me: I am employed in an honorary capacity (s 6(2)(c))`
    `the Act does not apply to me: I am not employed in the Territory (s 6(1))`
    `the Act does not apply to me: I do not work under a contract of service or apprenticeship, so I am not an employee (s 7(1))`

GIVEN `I am employed in the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another law provides my long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an award that applies to me provides for long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am employed in an honorary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved an agreement for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has exempted my employer for me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How the Act applies to me`
`ss 6, 7 -- how the Act applies` `I am employed in the Territory` `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `another law provides my long service leave` `an award that applies to me provides for long service leave` `I am employed in an honorary capacity` `the Minister has approved an agreement for me` `the Minister has exempted my employer for me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `I am employed in the Territory` THEN `the Act does not apply to me: I am not employed in the Territory (s 6(1))`
           IF `another law provides my long service leave` THEN `the Act does not apply to me: another law of the Territory, the Commonwealth or a State provides my long service leave (s 6(2)(a))`
           IF `an award that applies to me provides for long service leave` THEN `the Act does not apply to me: an award that applies to me provides for long service leave (s 6(2)(b))`
           IF `I am employed in an honorary capacity` THEN `the Act does not apply to me: I am employed in an honorary capacity (s 6(2)(c))`
           IF NOT `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` THEN `the Act does not apply to me: I do not work under a contract of service or apprenticeship, so I am not an employee (s 7(1))`
           IF `the Minister has exempted my employer for me` THEN `the Act applies to me, but the Minister has exempted my employer for me because a long service leave scheme gives me benefits no less favourable (s 13)`
           IF `the Minister has approved an agreement for me` THEN `the Act applies to me, but my long service leave is under the agreement the Minister approved (s 8(4), (5))`
           OTHERWISE `the Act applies to me`

@export Does the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 apply to me (ss 6, 7, 8(5), 13)? It covers employees in the Territory under a contract of service or apprenticeship (full-time, part-time, casual, piecework or outworker), unless another law or an award provides their long service leave or they work in an honorary capacity.
GIVEN `I am employed in the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or have been, employed in the Northern Territory
      `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work under a contract of service (employment) or apprenticeship with an employer, written, oral or implied, on salary, wages or piecework, full-time, part-time or casual, or as an outworker; being paid a share of the earnings, or hiring your tools or vehicle, does not stop you being an employee
      `another law provides my long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another law of the Territory, the Commonwealth or a State makes provision for your long service leave (for example a public service or a portable scheme Act)
      `an award that applies to me provides for long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, order, industrial agreement or common rule declaration that applies to you provides for long service leave (the Act's definition refers to the Workplace Relations Act 1996 of the Commonwealth)
      `I am employed in an honorary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work in an honorary (unpaid) capacity
      `the Minister has approved an agreement for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved, and not revoked, an agreement between you and your employer giving you long service leave benefits no less favourable than the Act's
      `the Minister has exempted my employer for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has exempted your employer from the Act, in writing, for you or a class of employees you belong to, because a scheme gives you benefits no less favourable
GIVETH A `How the Act applies to me`
`Does the Act apply to me` MEANS
    `ss 6, 7 -- how the Act applies` `I am employed in the Territory` `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `another law provides my long service leave` `an award that applies to me provides for long service leave` `I am employed in an honorary capacity` `the Minister has approved an agreement for me` `the Minister has exempted my employer for me`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Continuous service (s 12)`

-- s 12(1) "The period of qualifying service of an employee with an employer for the purposes of this Act is the period
-- during which the employee served ... continuously with the employer."
--
-- The completed years of continuous service from the first day of service, the last day counted, less the days of absence
-- that do not count (s 12(5)); the days that do not count push the first day later by as many days (fork F2).
GIVEN `the first day of my service` IS A DATE, `the day asked about` IS A DATE, `days that do not count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12 -- my completed years of continuous service` `the first day of my service` `the day asked about` `days that do not count` MEANS
    `the completed years from` (`the date` (`not below zero` `days that do not count`) `days after` `the first day of my service`) `to` `the day asked about`

@export How many completed years of continuous service with my employer do I have, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 12)? Counted from your first day of service (including service with a related company or a previous owner of the business, and an apprenticeship that counts), less absences that do not count; the other questions use this number.
GIVEN `the first day of my service` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your continuous service with your employer (or with a related company or previous owner of the business, or of an apprenticeship, if that service counts)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (today, or your last day of employment), counted as a day of service
      `days that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc The total days of absence that do not form part of your service (unpaid absences, stand-downs, disputes, gaps before re-employment; see the question on absences); 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many completed years of continuous service do I have` MEANS
    `s 12 -- my completed years of continuous service` `the first day of my service` `the day asked about` `days that do not count`

-- s 12(2) "an employee shall be deemed not to break ... continuity of service by reason of serving ...: (a) on continuous
-- full-time service in a part of the Reserve Forces or of the Citizen Forces; (b) in a part of those Forces for such period
-- as is ... fixed by or in accordance with regulations under the Defence Act 1903 ...; (c) on national service; or (d) as a
-- member of the Civil Construction Corps ..., and the period of service ... shall be deemed to be a period of employment".
-- s 12(4) "an employee shall be deemed not to break ... continuity of employment by reason of an interruption or
-- determination of that employment: (a) brought about by the action of the employer with the intention or result of
-- avoiding an obligation imposed on the employer by this Act; (b) arising directly or indirectly out of an industrial
-- dispute where the employee returns to his or her employment in accordance with the terms of settlement of the dispute;
-- (c) arising from the standing down of the employee by the employer for the reason of a slackness of trade; (d) after
-- completing a period of apprenticeship with the employer for a period not exceeding 12 months; or (e) for any other
-- reason and the employee was re-employed by that employer within 2 months of the interruption or determination."
DECLARE `Why my service was interrupted` IS ONE OF
    `I served in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps`
    `my employer ended or interrupted my employment to avoid, or with the result of avoiding, an obligation under the Act`
    `an industrial dispute`
    `my employer stood me down because of a slackness of trade`
    `I completed my apprenticeship with the employer`
    `another reason (including my resignation or dismissal)`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Why my service was interrupted`
      `I returned in accordance with the settlement of the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was interrupted` IS A DATE
      `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2), (4) -- my service stays continuous` `the reason` `I returned in accordance with the settlement of the dispute` `the day it was interrupted` `the day I was re-employed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `I served in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `my employer ended or interrupted my employment to avoid, or with the result of avoiding, an obligation under the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an industrial dispute` THEN
        IF `I returned in accordance with the settlement of the dispute`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE `re-employed within 2 months`
    WHEN `my employer stood me down because of a slackness of trade` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `I completed my apprenticeship with the employer` THEN
        `yes or no` (`the day` `the day I was re-employed` `is on or before` (`the same day` 12 `months after` `the day it was interrupted`))
    WHEN `another reason (including my resignation or dismissal)` THEN `re-employed within 2 months`
    WHERE
        -- s 12(4)(e) covers every reason; outside its 2 months the service is not "served continuously" (s 12(1)): fork F3.
        `re-employed within 2 months` MEANS
            `yes or no` (`the day` `the day I was re-employed` `is on or before` (`the same day` 2 `months after` `the day it was interrupted`))

@export Did a break in my employment keep my service continuous, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 12(2), (4))? Military or national service, an interruption by the employer to avoid the Act, an industrial dispute settled by your return, a stand-down for slackness of trade, re-employment within 12 months after an apprenticeship, or re-employment by the same employer within 2 months for any other reason does not break continuity.
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Why my service was interrupted` @desc Why your employment was interrupted or ended: you served in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps; your employer ended or interrupted it to avoid (or with the result of avoiding) an obligation under the Act; an industrial dispute; your employer stood you down because of a slackness of trade; you completed your apprenticeship with the employer; or another reason (including your resignation or dismissal)
      `I returned in accordance with the settlement of the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an industrial dispute, whether you returned to your employment in accordance with the terms of settlement of the dispute (otherwise answer no)
      `the day it was interrupted` IS A DATE @desc The day the employment was interrupted or ended (for an apprenticeship, the day you completed it)
      `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE @desc The day the same employer re-employed you, or you returned to work
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did the break keep my service continuous` MEANS
    `s 12(2), (4) -- my service stays continuous` `the reason` `I returned in accordance with the settlement of the dispute` `the day it was interrupted` `the day I was re-employed`

-- s 12(5) "Where an employee is or was absent otherwise than: (a) on leave granted with pay by the employer; or (b) by
-- action of the employer with the intention or result of avoiding an obligation imposed on the employer by this Act, the
-- period of the absence does not form part of the period of employment with that employer for the purposes of this Act."
-- s 12(2) closing words: military and like service "shall be deemed to be a period of employment".
DECLARE `Kind of absence` IS ONE OF
    `leave my employer granted with pay`
    `an absence my employer brought about to avoid, or with the result of avoiding, an obligation under the Act`
    `service in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps`
    `any other absence (unpaid leave, a stand-down, an industrial dispute, or the gap before I was re-employed)`

GIVEN `the absence` IS A `Kind of absence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2), (5) -- the absence counts as service` `the absence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the absence`
    WHEN `leave my employer granted with pay` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an absence my employer brought about to avoid, or with the result of avoiding, an obligation under the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `service in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other absence (unpaid leave, a stand-down, an industrial dispute, or the gap before I was re-employed)` THEN JUST FALSE

@export Does a period of absence count towards my years of service, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 12(2), (5))? Paid leave, an absence the employer caused to avoid the Act, and military or national service count; any other absence (unpaid leave, a stand-down, a dispute, a gap) does not count, even where it does not break continuity.
GIVEN `the absence` IS A `Kind of absence` @desc What the absence was: leave your employer granted with pay; an absence your employer brought about to avoid (or with the result of avoiding) an obligation under the Act; service in the Reserve Forces or Citizen Forces, on national service, or in the Civil Construction Corps; or any other absence (unpaid leave, a stand-down, an industrial dispute, or the gap before you were re-employed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the absence count towards my service` MEANS
    `s 12(2), (5) -- the absence counts as service` `the absence`

-- s 12(3) "Where an employee completes an apprenticeship with an employer and, within a period of 12 months after
-- completing that apprenticeship, the employee is re-employed by the employer, the period of that apprenticeship shall be
-- deemed to be a period of employment by the employee with the employer." A "where" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `the day I completed my apprenticeship` IS A DATE, `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(3) -- my apprenticeship counts` `the day I completed my apprenticeship` `the day I was re-employed` MEANS
    `yes or no` (    (`the day` `the day I completed my apprenticeship` `is on or before` `the day I was re-employed`)
                 AND (`the day` `the day I was re-employed` `is on or before` (`the same day` 12 `months after` `the day I completed my apprenticeship`)))

@export Does my apprenticeship count as service with my employer, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 12(3))? It counts if the same employer re-employed you within 12 months after you completed it.
GIVEN `the day I completed my apprenticeship` IS A DATE @desc The day you completed your apprenticeship with the employer
      `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE @desc The day the same employer re-employed you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my apprenticeship count` MEANS
    `s 12(3) -- my apprenticeship counts` `the day I completed my apprenticeship` `the day I was re-employed`

-- s 12(6) "Where an employee is employed in a corporation and, at any time prior, has been employed in one or more related
-- corporations and the periods of employment are continuous with one another ..., the sum of those periods ... shall ...
-- be included in the current period of employment". (7): related = subsidiary, holding or related corporation within the
-- Corporations Act 2001. (8) "Where: (a) all or part of a business, undertaking or establishment of an employer has ...
-- been transferred to another employer; and (b) a person who, at the time of the transfer, was an employee of the
-- first-mentioned employer and transfers his or her employment to that other employer, ... the period of employment with
-- the first-mentioned employer shall be deemed to be a period of employment with the other employer." (9) transfer
-- includes transmission, conveyance, assignment or succession, by agreement, will, administration or operation of law.
DECLARE `My earlier employer` IS ONE OF
    `a related corporation (a subsidiary, holding or related corporation under the Corporations Act 2001), with no break between the two`
    `the owner of the business, or part of it, before it was transferred to my present employer, and I moved with it`
    `another employer`

GIVEN `the earlier employer` IS A `My earlier employer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(6), (8) -- my earlier service counts` `the earlier employer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier employer`
    WHEN `a related corporation (a subsidiary, holding or related corporation under the Corporations Act 2001), with no break between the two` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the owner of the business, or part of it, before it was transferred to my present employer, and I moved with it` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- s 12(1): qualifying service "is the period during which the employee served ... continuously with the employer";
    -- outside s 12(6), (8) service with another employer is not service with this one (fork F4).
    WHEN `another employer` THEN JUST FALSE

@export Does my service with an earlier employer count towards my long service leave with my present employer, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 12(6) to (9))? Service with a related corporation, or with the previous owner of a business that was transferred to your present employer along with you, counts; service with any other employer does not.
GIVEN `the earlier employer` IS A `My earlier employer` @desc Who the earlier employer was: a related corporation (a subsidiary, holding or related corporation under the Corporations Act 2001), with no break between the two jobs; the owner of the business, or part of it, before it was transferred (sold, assigned, inherited or otherwise passed) to your present employer, where you moved with it; or another employer
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my earlier service count` MEANS
    `s 12(6), (8) -- my earlier service counts` `the earlier employer`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The entitlement (ss 6(4), 7(6), 8, 9)`

-- s 8(1) "Subject to this Act, where an employee has been employed by an employer for not less than 10 years continuous
-- service, the employee is entitled to long service leave, on pay calculated under section 11, for a period of 1.3 weeks
-- for each completed year of continuous service with the employer." A "where" condition: JUST FALSE under 10 years.
GIVEN `completed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) -- I am entitled to long service leave` `completed years` MEANS
    `yes or no` (FLOOR `completed years` AT LEAST 10)

@export Am I entitled to long service leave, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 8(1))? You are entitled once you have 10 years of continuous service with your employer.
GIVEN `completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed years of continuous service you have with your employer (see the question on completed years)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to long service leave` MEANS
    `s 8(1) -- I am entitled to long service leave` `completed years`

-- s 8(1): 1.3 weeks for each completed year, from 10 years; s 8(8) "the amount of long service leave due to that employee
-- is reduced by the period of the leave so granted"; s 7(6)(b) never more than 1.3 weeks a completed year; s 6(4) credit
-- only once for a period. This is the employee's "long service leave credit" (ss 10(1), 14(1)(c); undefined: fork F5).
GIVEN `completed years` IS A NUMBER, `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 8(1), (8) -- my long service leave credit in weeks` `completed years` `weeks already taken` MEANS
    IF FLOOR `completed years` AT LEAST 10
    THEN `not below zero` ((`weeks for each completed year` TIMES FLOOR `completed years`) MINUS `weeks already taken`)
    ELSE 0

@export How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 8(1), (8))? From 10 years of continuous service, 1.3 weeks for each completed year (13 weeks at 10 years, 19.5 at 15), less the leave already taken; none before 10 years. A public holiday during the leave is part of it and does not add a day (s 9).
GIVEN `completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed years of continuous service you have with your employer
      `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of long service leave under the Act you have already taken; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks of long service leave have I accrued` MEANS
    `s 8(1), (8) -- my long service leave credit in weeks` `completed years` `weeks already taken`

-- s 8(2) "... employed by an employer for a period of 10 years of continuous service, the employee is entitled to take long
-- service leave for a period equal to 1.3 weeks for each completed year of that 10 years continuous service." (3) "...
-- the employee becomes entitled to take long service leave on the completion of each subsequent period of 5 years
-- continuous service with that employer for a period equal to 1.3 weeks for each completed year of that 5 years ...".
-- So leave can be taken in blocks: 13 weeks at 10 years, 6.5 more at 15, 20, 25 ... (finding 1).
GIVEN `completed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 8(2), (3) -- the years whose leave I may take` `completed years` MEANS
    IF FLOOR `completed years` AT LEAST 10
    THEN 10 PLUS (5 TIMES FLOOR ((FLOOR `completed years` MINUS 10) DIVIDED BY 5))
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `completed years` IS A NUMBER, `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 8(2), (3), (8) -- the weeks I may take now` `completed years` `weeks already taken` MEANS
    `not below zero` ((`weeks for each completed year` TIMES `s 8(2), (3) -- the years whose leave I may take` `completed years`) MINUS `weeks already taken`)

@export How many weeks of long service leave can I take now, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 8(2), (3), (8))? The leave becomes available to take in blocks: 13 weeks after 10 years, then 6.5 weeks after each further 5 years (15, 20, 25 ...), less what you have already taken.
GIVEN `completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed years of continuous service you have with your employer
      `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of long service leave under the Act you have already taken; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks of long service leave can I take now` MEANS
    `s 8(2), (3), (8) -- the weeks I may take now` `completed years` `weeks already taken`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Taking the leave (s 8(6), (7), s 16)`

-- s 8(6) "... his or her employer shall grant and the employee shall take the long service leave ...: (a) as soon as
-- practicable after the leave has accrued, having regard to the needs of the employer's business, or commencing on and from
-- a date that is agreed upon ...; and (b) in one continuous period or, where the employer and employee agree, in separate
-- periods not exceeding 3, of not less than 4 weeks each." The when of (a) is a judgment (not asked); (b) is encoded.
GIVEN `number of periods` IS A NUMBER, `weeks in the shortest period` IS A NUMBER, `my employer and I agree to separate periods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(6)(b) -- I may take my leave in these periods` `number of periods` `weeks in the shortest period` `my employer and I agree to separate periods` MEANS
    `yes or no` (    (`number of periods` EQUALS 1)
                  OR (    `my employer and I agree to separate periods`
                      AND (`number of periods` AT MOST 3)
                      AND (`weeks in the shortest period` AT LEAST 4)))

@export Can I take my long service leave in separate periods, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 8(6)(b))? The leave is taken in one continuous period or, if you and your employer agree, in up to 3 separate periods of at least 4 weeks each.
GIVEN `number of periods` IS A NUMBER @desc Into how many periods the leave would be split (1 for one continuous period)
      `weeks in the shortest period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks the shortest of the periods would be
      `my employer and I agree to separate periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer agree to take the leave in separate periods
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I take my leave in these periods` MEANS
    `s 8(6)(b) -- I may take my leave in these periods` `number of periods` `weeks in the shortest period` `my employer and I agree to separate periods`

-- s 8(7) "Unless the employee otherwise agrees, an employer shall give to an employee not less than 2 months notice of the
-- date from which it is proposed that the employee's long service leave shall be granted and taken." Enough notice: the
-- start day is on or after the same day 2 months after the day of notice (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day I was given notice` IS A DATE, `the day the leave starts` IS A DATE, `I agreed to shorter notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) -- I was given enough notice` `the day I was given notice` `the day the leave starts` `I agreed to shorter notice` MEANS
    `yes or no` (    `I agreed to shorter notice`
                  OR (`the day` (`the same day` 2 `months after` `the day I was given notice`) `is on or before` `the day the leave starts`))

@export Did my employer give me enough notice of when my long service leave starts, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 8(7))? Unless you agree otherwise, your employer must give you at least 2 months notice of the day the leave is to start.
GIVEN `the day I was given notice` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer told you the day your leave is to start
      `the day the leave starts` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the leave
      `I agreed to shorter notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed to less than 2 months notice (or to that start day)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I given enough notice of my leave` MEANS
    `s 8(7) -- I was given enough notice` `the day I was given notice` `the day the leave starts` `I agreed to shorter notice`

-- s 16 "An employee shall not, during any period while on long service leave granted by the employer under this Act, engage
-- in any other remunerative employment with duties of a kind performed by the employee in the employment from which leave
-- was granted." s 18(1): maximum penalty 8 penalty units or imprisonment for 6 months. The prohibition is limited by its
-- own wording; other work it does not forbid: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the work is paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the duties are of the kind I do in my job` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 -- the Act forbids the other work` `the work is paid` `the duties are of the kind I do in my job` MEANS
    IF `the work is paid` AND `the duties are of the kind I do in my job`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 16 forbids only paid employment with duties of the same kind)

@export Does the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 forbid me to take other work while I am on long service leave (s 16)? It forbids other paid employment with duties of the kind you do in the job you are on leave from (maximum penalty 8 penalty units or 6 months imprisonment, s 18(1)); it says nothing about other work.
GIVEN `the work is paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other work is paid employment
      `the duties are of the kind I do in my job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether its duties are of a kind you perform in the job you are on leave from
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the Act forbid the other work during my leave` MEANS
    `s 16 -- the Act forbids the other work` `the work is paid` `the duties are of the kind I do in my job`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `When my employment ends, or I die (s 10) -- arises only when the employment ends`

-- s 10(1) "Subject to subsection (1A), where an employee who is entitled to long service leave ceases to be an employee
-- otherwise than by death, the employer is to pay to the employee the amount payable under section 11 for a period equal
-- to the period of his or her long service leave credit at the time he or she ceases that employment."
-- (1A) "Where an employee who is entitled to long service leave ceases to be an employee by reason of serious misconduct,
-- the employer shall pay ..., in lieu of long service leave, an amount not less than the amount that would be payable ...
-- under section 11 for his or her long service leave credit ... (if any) in respect of: (a) where the employee has completed
-- not less than 10, but less than 15 years, ..., the completed period of 10 years continuous service only; and (b) where
-- the employee has completed not less than 15 years ..., completed periods of 5 years continuous service only."
-- (2) "Where an employee whose period of employment is less than 10 years but not less than 7 years ceases to be an
-- employee of that employer, otherwise than by death: (a) on or subsequent to attaining the age at which he or she may
-- retire; (b) on the termination of employment by the employer for a reason other than serious misconduct; or (c) on
-- account of illness, incapacity or domestic or other pressing necessity of such a nature as to justify so ceasing to be
-- an employee, the employer shall pay to the employee the amount payable under section 11 for a period equal to 1.3 weeks
-- for each completed year of service of that employment."
-- (3) "Where an employee dies and would have been entitled to payment under subsection (1) or (2) had he or she otherwise
-- ceased to be employed on the date of death, the employer shall, on the request of the personal representative ...,
-- pay to the personal representative the amount that would have been payable to the employee under those circumstances."
-- (4) "Except as provided by this section, an employer shall not pay to an employee, and an employee shall not accept, any
-- amount in lieu of long service leave to which the employee is entitled under this Act."
DECLARE `How my employment ended` IS ONE OF
    `I resigned`
    `my employer ended my employment for a reason other than serious misconduct`
    `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct`
    `I left on account of illness, incapacity, or domestic or other pressing necessity that justified leaving`
    `I died`

-- The weeks of pay owed. Weeks already taken are taken off every head (s 6(4), s 7(6)(a); fork F6). Under s 10(1A) the
-- figure is the least the employer must pay ("not less than").
GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended`
      `completed years` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER
      `I had reached the age at which I may retire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10 -- the weeks of pay owed when my employment ends` `how it ended` `completed years` `weeks already taken` `I had reached the age at which I may retire` MEANS
    IF `years` AT LEAST 10
    THEN CONSIDER `how it ended`
         WHEN `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct` THEN
             JUST (`not below zero` ((`weeks for each completed year` TIMES `the years in completed 5-year periods`) MINUS `weeks already taken`))
         OTHERWISE JUST (`s 8(1), (8) -- my long service leave credit in weeks` `years` `weeks already taken`)
    ELSE IF `years` AT LEAST 7
         THEN IF `I had reached the age at which I may retire`
              THEN JUST `the s 10(2) weeks`
              ELSE CONSIDER `how it ended`
                   WHEN `my employer ended my employment for a reason other than serious misconduct` THEN JUST `the s 10(2) weeks`
                   WHEN `I left on account of illness, incapacity, or domestic or other pressing necessity that justified leaving` THEN JUST `the s 10(2) weeks`
                   -- s 10(3) asks what s 10(2) would have given "had he or she otherwise ceased to be employed on the date
                   -- of death"; under retirement age, which head of s 10(2) would apply is not said (finding 4).
                   WHEN `I died` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 10(3) does not say how the employee is taken to have ceased)
                   -- Resignation, or dismissal for serious misconduct, under 10 years: s 10(4) forbids any payment in lieu.
                   OTHERWISE JUST 0
         ELSE JUST 0
    WHERE
        `years` MEANS FLOOR `completed years`
        `the years in completed 5-year periods` MEANS
            IF `years` LESS THAN 15
            THEN 10
            ELSE 5 TIMES FLOOR (`years` DIVIDED BY 5)
        `the s 10(2) weeks` MEANS `not below zero` ((`weeks for each completed year` TIMES `years`) MINUS `weeks already taken`)

@export How many weeks of long service leave pay must I (or my estate) be paid when my employment ends, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 10)? From 10 years, the leave not yet taken (1.3 weeks a completed year); after dismissal for serious misconduct, at least the leave for completed 10- and 5-year blocks; between 7 and 10 years, 1.3 weeks a year if you reached retirement age, were terminated other than for serious misconduct, or left for illness, incapacity or pressing necessity; otherwise none. On a death the personal representative must ask for it.
GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended` @desc How your employment ended: you resigned; your employer ended it for a reason other than serious misconduct; your employer dismissed you for serious misconduct; you left on account of illness, incapacity, or domestic or other pressing necessity that justified leaving; or you died (asked by your personal representative)
      `completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed years of continuous service you had with the employer when the employment ended
      `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of long service leave under the Act you had already taken; 0 if none
      `I had reached the age at which I may retire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment ended on or after you reached the age at which you may retire
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How many weeks of pay must I be paid when my employment ends` MEANS
    `s 10 -- the weeks of pay owed when my employment ends` `how it ended` `completed years` `weeks already taken` `I had reached the age at which I may retire`

-- s 10(4) "Except as provided by this section, an employer shall not pay to an employee, and an employee shall not accept,
-- any amount in lieu of long service leave to which the employee is entitled under this Act." s 7(6)(a): no more than one
-- payment. While the employment continues, no cash in place of leave: JUST FALSE (flat negative).
GIVEN `my employment is ending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(4) -- I may be paid out instead of taking leave` `my employment is ending` MEANS
    `yes or no` `my employment is ending`

@export Can my employer pay me money instead of my taking long service leave, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 10(4))? Only when your employment ends, as section 10 provides; while you stay employed your employer must not pay, and you must not accept, money in place of the leave.
GIVEN `my employment is ending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment would be made because your employment is ending (or you have died)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be paid out instead of taking leave` MEANS
    `s 10(4) -- I may be paid out instead of taking leave` `my employment is ending`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `How much I am paid (ss 7(2), (4), 11)`

-- s 11(2) "... the amount payable to the employee is the sum of the amounts calculated under subsection (3) for each
-- completed year of continuous service that comprises the period of service from which his or her entitlement to long
-- service leave is derived." (3) "... the formula RP x HWW x 1.3, where: RP means an employee's rate of pay payable on the
-- day immediately preceding the day on which he or she ceases to be an employee or takes a period of long service leave,
-- or on the day as agreed in accordance with subsection (8)(a) ...; HWW means the number of hours of work per week an
-- employee worked for an employer during a year of the continuous service."
GIVEN `rate of pay` IS A NUMBER, `hours of work per week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11(3) -- the amount for one completed year` `rate of pay` `hours of work per week` MEANS
    `rate of pay` TIMES `hours of work per week` TIMES `weeks for each completed year`

GIVEN `rate of pay` IS A NUMBER, `hours in each year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11(2) -- the amount payable` `rate of pay` `hours in each year` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN h YIELD `s 11(3) -- the amount for one completed year` `rate of pay` h) `hours in each year`)

@export How much must I be paid for my long service leave, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 11(2), (3))? For each completed year of service the leave is drawn from: your hourly rate of pay x the hours of work per week you worked that year x 1.3. For example $15 an hour and 40 hours a week for 10 years gives $7,800 (s 11(4)).
GIVEN `rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Your hourly rate of pay, in dollars, on the day before your leave starts or your employment ends (or on the day agreed for postponed leave under s 11(8)(a)), overtime and penalty rates left out
      `hours in each year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each completed year of service the payment is for, the hours of work per week you worked that year (fixed hours, or the average), overtime left out; one number per year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must I be paid for my long service leave` MEANS
    `s 11(2) -- the amount payable` `rate of pay` `hours in each year`

-- The same where the hours were the same in every year: RP x HWW x (1.3 x years) = RP x HWW x weeks.
@export How much is a number of weeks of my long service leave pay, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 11(3)), where my weekly hours were the same in every year? The hourly rate of pay x the hours of work per week x the weeks (1.3 for each completed year).
GIVEN `rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Your hourly rate of pay, in dollars, on the day before your leave starts or your employment ends, overtime and penalty rates left out
      `hours of work per week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours of work per week you worked, the same in every year counted, overtime left out
      `weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc The weeks of long service leave (see the questions on accrued leave and on the end of employment)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my pay for these weeks of leave` MEANS
    `rate of pay` TIMES `hours of work per week` TIMES `weeks`

-- s 11(1) "rate of pay means an employee's remuneration for the hours of work per week ... calculated: (a) ... where
-- remunerated in accordance with a rate of pay fixed by the terms of employment ..., that rate of pay; or (b) [otherwise]
-- the average rate of pay paid to the employee during a year of continuous service (to be calculated by dividing the
-- total amount of pay paid, other than any amount paid for hours of overtime worked or as district allowance, site
-- allowance, climatic allowance or penalty rates, by the total number of hours, other than hours of overtime, worked by
-- the employee during the year of continuous service)." s 7(4): pay and commission over the year are added together.
GIVEN `my rate is fixed by my terms of employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fixed rate` IS A NUMBER, `pay in the year` IS A NUMBER, `hours in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(1) -- my rate of pay` `my rate is fixed by my terms of employment` `the fixed rate` `pay in the year` `hours in the year` MEANS
    IF `my rate is fixed by my terms of employment`
    THEN JUST `the fixed rate`
    ELSE IF `hours in the year` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN JUST (`pay in the year` DIVIDED BY `hours in the year`)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: with no ordinary hours in the year the average divides by zero)

@export What is my rate of pay for long service leave, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 11(1))? The hourly rate fixed by your terms of employment; otherwise (commission, piecework, a mix) the average over the year: pay (with commission, without overtime, penalty rates and district, site or climatic allowances) divided by the hours worked other than overtime.
GIVEN `my rate is fixed by my terms of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid wholly at an hourly rate fixed by your terms of employment
      `the fixed rate` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that hourly rate in dollars (otherwise 0)
      `pay in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If not, the total pay, in dollars, you were paid in the year of continuous service, commission included, leaving out overtime, penalty rates and district, site or climatic allowances (otherwise 0)
      `hours in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If not, the total hours you worked in that year, leaving out overtime (otherwise 0)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my rate of pay` MEANS
    `s 11(1) -- my rate of pay` `my rate is fixed by my terms of employment` `the fixed rate` `pay in the year` `hours in the year`

-- s 11(1) "hours of work per week means: (a) the fixed number of hours per week an employee has worked ... during a year of
-- continuous service ...; or (b) where an employee has not worked a fixed number of hours per week, the average number of
-- hours per week the employee has worked ... during a year of continuous service ..., but does not include hours of
-- overtime". The average is taken over the 52 weeks of the year (fork F7).
GIVEN `my hours were fixed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fixed hours` IS A NUMBER, `hours in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11(1) -- my hours of work per week` `my hours were fixed` `the fixed hours` `hours in the year` MEANS
    IF `my hours were fixed`
    THEN `the fixed hours`
    ELSE `hours in the year` DIVIDED BY 52

@export What were my hours of work per week in a year of service, for long service leave pay under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 11(1))? The fixed weekly hours you worked; if they were not fixed, the average over the year; overtime is left out.
GIVEN `my hours were fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you worked a fixed number of hours each week in that year
      `the fixed hours` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the fixed hours per week, without overtime (otherwise 0)
      `hours in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If not, the total hours you worked in that year, without overtime (otherwise 0)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What were my hours of work per week` MEANS
    `s 11(1) -- my hours of work per week` `my hours were fixed` `the fixed hours` `hours in the year`

-- s 7(2) "A reference in this Act to an employee's pay shall be read as including a reference to: (a) an over-award payment,
-- industry, leading hand, skill or qualification allowance or service grant; (b) any amounts payable ... under a bonus or
-- incentive scheme, being amounts that are usually paid to the employee with his or her pay; (c) [free board or lodging];
-- and (d) any allowance of a specified kind prescribed by the Regulations ..., but not including a reference to district
-- allowance, site allowance, climatic allowance or any other allowance or payment in respect of overtime or penalty rates
-- of pay." (4) pay and commission are added together.
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `an over-award payment`
    `an industry, leading hand, skill or qualification allowance`
    `a service grant`
    `a bonus or incentive payment usually paid with my pay`
    `a bonus or incentive payment not usually paid with my pay`
    `free board or lodging from my employer`
    `commission`
    `a district, site or climatic allowance`
    `overtime pay or penalty rates`
    `another allowance`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Kind of payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2), (4) -- the payment is part of my pay` `the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `an over-award payment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an industry, leading hand, skill or qualification allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a service grant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a bonus or incentive payment usually paid with my pay` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a bonus or incentive payment not usually paid with my pay` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open definition: s 7(2) "shall be read as including"; (b) reaches only amounts usually paid with the pay)
    WHEN `free board or lodging from my employer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `commission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a district, site or climatic allowance` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `overtime pay or penalty rates` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another allowance` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open definition: s 7(2)(d) lets the Regulations add allowances; they are not deposited)

@export Does this payment count as part of my pay for long service leave, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 7(2), (4))? Over-award payments, industry, leading hand, skill or qualification allowances, service grants, bonuses usually paid with your pay, free board or lodging and commission count; district, site and climatic allowances, overtime and penalty rates do not.
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Kind of payment` @desc The kind of payment: an over-award payment; an industry, leading hand, skill or qualification allowance; a service grant; a bonus or incentive payment usually paid with your pay; a bonus or incentive payment not usually paid with your pay; free board or lodging from your employer; commission; a district, site or climatic allowance; overtime pay or penalty rates; or another allowance
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does this payment count as part of my pay` MEANS
    `s 7(2), (4) -- the payment is part of my pay` `the payment`

-- s 7(2)(c) "if the employee is provided with free board or lodging by the employer -- an amount equal to the value of that
-- board or lodging fixed by or under the terms of employment or, if not so fixed, $15 per week for board or $5 per week for
-- lodging".
GIVEN `I get free board` IS A BOOLEAN, `I get free lodging` IS A BOOLEAN, `the value is fixed by my terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fixed weekly value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7(2)(c) -- the weekly value of board and lodging` `I get free board` `I get free lodging` `the value is fixed by my terms` `the fixed weekly value` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`I get free board` OR `I get free lodging`))
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the value is fixed by my terms`
         THEN `the fixed weekly value`
         ELSE `board` PLUS `lodging`
    WHERE
        `board` MEANS IF `I get free board` THEN 15 ELSE 0
        `lodging` MEANS IF `I get free lodging` THEN 5 ELSE 0

@export What weekly amount for free board or lodging counts as part of my pay for long service leave, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 7(2)(c))? The value fixed by your terms of employment; if none is fixed, $15 a week for board and $5 a week for lodging.
GIVEN `I get free board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer gives you free board (meals)
      `I get free lodging` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer gives you free lodging (accommodation)
      `the value is fixed by my terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your terms of employment fix a value for the board or lodging
      `the fixed weekly value` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that weekly value in dollars (otherwise 0)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What weekly amount for board or lodging counts as pay` MEANS
    `s 7(2)(c) -- the weekly value of board and lodging` `I get free board` `I get free lodging` `the value is fixed by my terms` `the fixed weekly value`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `When I must be paid (s 11(6) to (8))`

-- The parties and acts of the rules with deadlines.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `my employer`, `me`
DECLARE `What is done` IS ONE OF
    `pay my long service leave` HAS `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay my personal representative` HAS `the amount paid to the estate` IS A NUMBER

-- s 11(6) "Subject to subsection (8), where an employee is to take a period of long service leave, his or her employer is
-- to pay the amount calculated under (2) to the employee in respect of the whole of the period: (a) on or before the last
-- day on which the employee is required to work before he or she commences the leave; or (b) on the pay day immediately
-- before he or she commences the leave, as agreed between the employer and employee." (8)(b) they may agree another time.
-- Day 0 is the day the leave was fixed; the employer MUST pay the whole amount WITHIN the days to the day it is due.
-- A payment of less than the whole amount does not count.
GIVEN `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
`s 11(6) -- pay the whole of the leave before it starts` `the amount owed` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `my employer`
    MUST `pay my long service leave` `the amount` PROVIDED `the amount` AT LEAST `the amount owed`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `my employer` BECAUSE "the whole of the long service leave pay was not paid by the last working day, or the pay day, before the leave began, or the other time agreed (s 11(6), (8)(b))"

-- s 11(7) "Where an employee ceases to be an employee on retirement, termination of employment, ill health, death or
-- domestic or other pressing necessity, the employer is to pay the amount calculated under subsection (2): (a) to the
-- employee as soon as practicable after termination of his or her employment; or (b) in the case of a deceased employee,
-- to his or her personal representative as soon as practicable after the death of the employee, but in any case not later
-- than 12 months after his or her death." Day 0 is the death; "as soon as practicable" is a judgment, not encoded; the
-- outer limit is the same day 12 months on (fork F1).
GIVEN `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER, `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
`s 11(7)(b) -- pay the estate within 12 months of the death` `the amount owed` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `my employer`
    MUST `pay my personal representative` `the amount` PROVIDED `the amount` AT LEAST `the amount owed`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `my employer` BECAUSE "the long service leave pay was not paid to the personal representative within 12 months after the death (s 11(7)(b))"

-- The helper that runs a rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but
-- not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
      `the party` IS A `Party`
      `the act` IS A `What is done`
      `the day it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `done in time under` `the rule` `by` `the party` `doing` `the act` `on day` `the day it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day it was done`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the day it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Whether I was paid on time` IS ONE OF
    `paid in full on time`
    `paid in full, but late`
    `not yet paid in full, and not yet due`
    `not yet paid in full, and overdue`

GIVEN `the day the leave was fixed` IS A DATE
      `the day it was due` IS A DATE
      `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the day it was paid` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Whether I was paid on time`
`s 11(6) -- whether my leave pay was paid on time` `the day the leave was fixed` `the day it was due` `the amount owed` `the amount paid` `the day it was paid` `today` MEANS
    IF `the amount paid` AT LEAST `the amount owed`
    THEN IF `done in time under` (`s 11(6) -- pay the whole of the leave before it starts` `the amount owed` (`not below zero` (`the days from` `the day the leave was fixed` `to` `the day it was due`))) `by` `my employer` `doing` (`pay my long service leave` `the amount paid`) `on day` (`not below zero` (`the days from` `the day the leave was fixed` `to` `the day it was paid`))
         THEN `paid in full on time`
         ELSE `paid in full, but late`
    ELSE IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` `the day it was due`
         THEN `not yet paid in full, and not yet due`
         ELSE `not yet paid in full, and overdue`

@export Was my long service leave pay paid on time before my leave, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 11(6), (8))? The whole amount for the leave is due on or before your last working day before the leave, or on the pay day before it, as you and your employer agreed (or at another time you agreed in writing or otherwise).
GIVEN `the day the leave was fixed` IS A DATE @desc The day the dates of your leave were fixed (agreed or notified)
      `the day it was due` IS A DATE @desc The day the pay was due: your last working day before the leave, or the pay day immediately before it, as agreed, or another day you and your employer agreed
      `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount owed for the whole period of leave, in dollars (see the questions on how much)
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you have been paid for it, in dollars; 0 if nothing
      `the day it was paid` IS A DATE @desc The day it was paid (any day if nothing has been paid)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Whether I was paid on time`
`Was my leave pay paid on time` MEANS
    `s 11(6) -- whether my leave pay was paid on time` `the day the leave was fixed` `the day it was due` `the amount owed` `the amount paid` `the day it was paid` `today`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 11(7)(b) -- the last day to pay the estate` `the day of death` MEANS `the same day` 12 `months after` `the day of death`

@export By when must the employer pay a deceased employee's long service leave to the personal representative, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 11(7)(b))? As soon as practicable after the death, and in any case not later than 12 months after it; this gives that last day.
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the employee died
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my estate be paid` MEANS
    `s 11(7)(b) -- the last day to pay the estate` `the day of death`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the day it was paid` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Whether I was paid on time`
`s 11(7)(b) -- whether the estate was paid on time` `the day of death` `the amount owed` `the amount paid` `the day it was paid` `today` MEANS
    IF `the amount paid` AT LEAST `the amount owed`
    THEN IF `done in time under` (`s 11(7)(b) -- pay the estate within 12 months of the death` `the amount owed` (`the days from` `the day of death` `to` `the last day`)) `by` `my employer` `doing` (`pay my personal representative` `the amount paid`) `on day` (`not below zero` (`the days from` `the day of death` `to` `the day it was paid`))
         THEN `paid in full on time`
         ELSE `paid in full, but late`
    ELSE IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` `the last day`
         THEN `not yet paid in full, and not yet due`
         ELSE `not yet paid in full, and overdue`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `s 11(7)(b) -- the last day to pay the estate` `the day of death`

@export Was a deceased employee's long service leave paid to the personal representative within the 12 months the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 allows (s 11(7)(b))? Asked by the personal representative; "not yet due" means the 12 months have not run out, though the employer must pay as soon as practicable.
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the employee died
      `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount owed to the estate for long service leave, in dollars
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the employer has paid you as personal representative, in dollars; 0 if nothing
      `the day it was paid` IS A DATE @desc The day it was paid (any day if nothing has been paid)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Whether I was paid on time`
`Was my estate paid on time` MEANS
    `s 11(7)(b) -- whether the estate was paid on time` `the day of death` `the amount owed` `the amount paid` `the day it was paid` `today`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Records, offences and enforcement (ss 14, 17, 18, 18A)`

-- s 14(2) "An employer shall retain a record referred to in subsection (1): (a) after the date on which the employee to
-- whom the record relates ceased to be employed by the employer -- until the expiration of 3 years; and (b) in the case of
-- an employee whose employment is terminated by death -- 6 years after the date on which all moneys owing to the legal
-- personal representative are paid." The record (s 14(1)) shows the name, start date, wages, prior qualifying service,
-- weekly hours, the accrued credit, leave taken or paid, absences of 2 months or more, and the day employment ended.
GIVEN `the employee died` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the employment ended` IS A DATE, `the day all moneys were paid to the estate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 14(2) -- the record must be kept until` `the employee died` `the day the employment ended` `the day all moneys were paid to the estate` MEANS
    IF `the employee died`
    THEN `the same day` 6 `years after` `the day all moneys were paid to the estate`
    ELSE `the same day` 3 `years after` `the day the employment ended`

@export Until when must my former employer keep my long service leave records, under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 (s 14(2))? For 3 years after your employment ended; if the employee died, 6 years after all money owed to the personal representative was paid.
GIVEN `the employee died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment ended because the employee died
      `the day the employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the employment ended
      `the day all moneys were paid to the estate` IS A DATE @desc If the employee died, the day all money owed to the personal representative was paid (otherwise any day)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when must my leave records be kept` MEANS
    `s 14(2) -- the record must be kept until` `the employee died` `the day the employment ended` `the day all moneys were paid to the estate`

-- s 17(1) "This Act has effect notwithstanding any employment agreement that confers on the employee rights that are not
-- as advantageous to the employee as the rights conferred on an employee by this Act." Subject to an agreement approved
-- under s 8(5) (s 8(4)). A term less advantageous does not take away the Act's rights; the Act is silent on a term that
-- is as advantageous or more (it can stand beside the Act, subject to s 8(4)).
GIVEN `the term is less advantageous to me than the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- my Act rights stand despite the agreement` `the term is less advantageous to me than the Act` `the Minister approved the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the Minister approved the agreement`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the term is less advantageous to me than the Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 17(1) speaks only of rights not as advantageous as the Act's)

@export Do my rights under the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 stand even though my employment agreement gives me less (s 17(1))? Yes: the Act has effect despite an agreement that is less advantageous to you, unless the Minister approved the agreement under s 8(5).
GIVEN `the term is less advantageous to me than the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term of your employment agreement gives you long service leave rights less advantageous than the Act's
      `the Minister approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister approved the agreement under s 8(5) (as no less favourable than the Act)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do my rights stand despite my agreement` MEANS
    `s 17(1) -- my Act rights stand despite the agreement` `the term is less advantageous to me than the Act` `the Minister approved the agreement`

-- s 18(1) "A person shall not contravene or fail to comply with a provision of this Act. Maximum penalty: 8 penalty units
-- or imprisonment for 6 months." (2) on a finding of guilt the court may also order the person found guilty to pay what
-- is due to the employee. s 18A "... a proceeding for an offence against this Act may be instituted within 3 years after
-- the act or omission alleged to constitute the offence."
`s 18(1) -- the maximum penalty in penalty units` MEANS 8
`s 18(1) -- the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 6

GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 18A -- the last day to prosecute` `the day of the act or omission` MEANS `the same day` 3 `years after` `the day of the act or omission`

@export By when can my employer be prosecuted for failing to give me what the Northern Territory's Long Service Leave Act 1981 requires (s 18A)? Within 3 years after the act or failure. The maximum penalty is 8 penalty units or 6 months imprisonment, and the court may also order the employer to pay you what is due (s 18).
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the employer's act or failure (for example the day leave pay was due and not paid)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when can my employer be prosecuted` MEANS
    `s 18A -- the last day to prosecute` `the day of the act or omission`
